  "source_quote": "Uncontrolled hyperglycaemia with a glucose level >240 mg/dl (>13.3 mmol/L) after an overnight fast during placebo run-in and confirmed by a second measurement (not on the same day)",
  "predicate": {
    "type": "unsupported",
    "reason": "This is not a single-timepoint lab threshold: it requires an initial fasting glucose >240 mg/dl during a specific study phase ('placebo run-in', not one of the resolvable anchors: screening/enrolment/randomisation/consent/first_dose) plus a confirmatory second measurement on a different day. The confirmation-by-repeat-testing requirement is a process, not a chart state, and the run-in-phase anchor cannot be mapped onto the screening-anchored window model without changing its meaning."
  },
  "notes": "Declining rather than approximating as a simple observation >240 mg/dl, because doing so would drop the mandatory second-measurement confirmation and misrepresent the placebo-run-in timing as a screening-relative window."
